# ⛔ NOT *.summary.  BUILD-AND-DEPLOY.md §5 requires BigMig.fit.summary to be archived
# beside every .rbf we keep -- that rule exists because a month of fitter reports was lost
# and a bitstream could no longer be compared against the one it replaced.  A blanket
# ignore here silently defeats it: the artefacts get committed, the reports do not.
output_files/*.summary
*.done
*.jdi
*.pin
*.sof
*.qws
*.ppf
*.ddb
build_id.v
c5_pin_model_dump.txt
*.sopcinfo
*.csv
*.f
*.cmp
*.sip
*.spd
*.bsf
*~
*.xml
*_netlist
# ⛔ NOT *.cdf.  BigMig.qsf:222 assigns CDF_FILE jtag.cdf, so it is a PROJECT INPUT and a
# clone without it is incomplete.  (extra/clean.bat also deletes *.cdf -- same trap.)
output_files/*.cdf

# local lint/sim scratch binaries
sys/lw_wrap
sys/*.o

# deployable artifacts (Drive-visible, not tracked)
# builds/ was the old catch-all artefact folder; it is gone (2026-08-12), split into
# internal_builds_ship / _diag / _experiments.  Those are TRACKED on purpose -- this repo
# is the internal matrix and keeps its own artefacts.  They never travel to the public
# repo, and that is enforced by SELECTION (internal_harness/PUBLICATION-CONTRACT.md 4),
# not by .gitignore.
builds/
.DS_Store

# The release set is staged here and published as a GitHub *Release* (assets), not as
# repo content -- it keeps the clone light and the binaries versioned by tag instead.
# ⚠ This is the one legitimate use of .gitignore in this repo: nothing is being hidden,
# a build product is simply not tracked.  Internal material is kept out by SELECTION
# (Toolkit-DE10/public-tree-check.py), never by exclusion.
releases/
